      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "DIAMOND EYE (2) gets the nod after a solid second at Ballarat on heavy ground, where she was sent out favourite and fought on without ever really threatening Torn. The quick back-up suits, she has already won at this track, and Damian Lane aboard adds to the confidence. CUSHIONED (4) is a danger if she rebounds from a BM70 failure at Bendigo, where she was beaten a long way after being eased from the 300m. Her Cranbourne fourth the start prior was much better, with traffic late, and the drop from BM70 grade keeps her firmly in play. MAHMUDAH (3) brings the neatest winning form, having beaten Monsun's Pride at Kilmore in a BM56 as a well-supported favourite, though this is a stronger assignment. FINE AND SUNNY (7) was decisive when winning a Pakenham Mdn by two lengths on soft ground and, while this is a bigger test, that win gives her something to build on.",
